AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002129> "The circuits in the cerebellar cortex look similar across all classes of vertebrates, including fish, reptiles, birds, and mammals (e.g., Fig. 2). This has been taken as evidence that the cerebellum performs functions important to all vertebrate species. (Wikipedia)")
